# Copy this file to ".env" and paste your keys after the "=" signs.
# NEVER commit .env — it is already in .gitignore.
# Every key below is free. SETUP.md walks through getting each one, in order.
# The project runs without any of them (it falls back to no-key sources);
# the keys unlock extra series and higher rate limits.

# 1) FRED — macro series (repair CPI, diesel, used-car CPI, VMT).
#    https://fredaccount.stlouisfed.org/apikeys   (32-character lowercase string)
FRED_API_KEY=

# 2) BLS — Bureau of Labor Statistics v2 API (higher limits than the keyless v1).
#    https://data.bls.gov/registrationEngine/
BLS_API_KEY=

# 3) EIA — weekly on-highway diesel prices.
#    https://www.eia.gov/opendata/register.php
EIA_API_KEY=

# 4) US Census — International Trade API, used-vehicle exports by country/port.
#    https://api.census.gov/data/key_signup.html
CENSUS_API_KEY=

# 5) SEC EDGAR — no key, but the SEC REQUIRES a descriptive User-Agent with a
#    real email or it returns 403. Put your own name and email here.
SEC_USER_AGENT=Copart AltData Research (your.name@utexas.edu)
